question 2    Create a UDP client on a node nl and a UDP server on a node n2.

Aim:
To create a UDP client on node n1 and a UDP server on node n2.

Procedure:

Create two nodes named n1 and n2.
Attach a UDP Agent to node n1.
Attach a Null Agent (UDP Server) to node n2.
Connect the UDP client with the UDP server.
Attach a CBR (Constant Bit Rate) traffic source to the UDP client.
Start the simulation and observe the packet transmission.

Observation:

The UDP client sends packets from n1 to n2.
The UDP server receives the packets.
UDP is a connectionless protocol and does not require acknowledgements.
Packet delivery is faster but not guaranteed.

Result:
The UDP client was successfully created on node n1, and the UDP server was successfully created on node n2. Data packets were transmitted successfully between the two nodes.




